WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:03.189
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here.

00:00:03.189 --> 00:00:06.800
If you've watched my review of Moana, you'll
know I really enjoyed the animated feature.

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:10.309
So, in this video, I want to look at the five
funniest moments from the film.

00:00:10.309 --> 00:00:13.829
Obviously, there are spoilers ahead if you
haven't seen the film already!

00:00:13.829 --> 00:00:18.199
And if that's you, you can check out my spoiler-free
review of the movie here, and come back and

00:00:18.199 --> 00:00:19.820
watch this video after you've seen it!

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:25.010
By the way, I've got a fab giveaway to win
this gorgeous Art of Moana hardback book.

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:30.109
It'll be on my Moana Easter Egg video, so
make sure you subscribe and I'll add a link

00:00:30.109 --> 00:00:31.980
here to the video when it's ready.

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:36.530
Kicking us off at number five is the scene
where Maui steals Moana's boat and sails off,

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:40.570
even taking along Moana's rooster side-kick,
Heihei, as a snack for later!

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:44.629
It's especially funny when Moana escapes from
the cave where the trickster demi-god trapped

00:00:44.629 --> 00:00:49.449
her and launches herself into the air to try
and catch up with Maui on the boat, but just

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:51.550
misses it and lands splat in the sea.

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:56.160
And I love how Maui reacts, saying, 'I could
watch that all day.

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:57.289
Ok, enjoy the island.

00:00:57.289 --> 00:01:01.969
Maui out!', then he tries to get away, but
the ocean has other ideas and carries Moana

00:01:01.969 --> 00:01:07.700
back on to the canoe again and again, despite
Maui's repeated attempts to get rid of her!

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:11.900
It's just a little slapstick scene, but it's
still very amusing when Heihei stows away

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:15.090
on Moana's boat and she finds him once they've
set sail.

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:20.079
That moment is so funny when Moana takes the
half-coconut shell off Heihei's head and he

00:01:20.079 --> 00:01:26.250
realises where he actually is, not on dry
land with rocks to peck and swallow, but surrounded

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:30.930
by water in the middle of the ocean, and he
lets out a piercing scream, which only stops

00:01:30.930 --> 00:01:38.370
each time Moana puts the coconut shell back
on his head!

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:48.170
I love the magnificently crazy action scene
where a boat-load of teeny-tiny pirates wearing

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:52.100
armour made of coconut shells attack Moana
and Maui on the high seas!

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:57.350
There's so many of them that they're absolutely
everywhere, zip-lining on to Moana's boat,

00:01:57.350 --> 00:02:01.500
swiping Heihei who's swallowed the heart of
Te Fiti, and suddenly turning their one ship

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:02.500
into three!

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:06.630
There's loads of fun in this fast-paced scene,
including the Kakamoras accidentally shooting

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:08.640
their chief with a blow-dart!

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:14.110
And Moana gets some bad-ass action fighting
the coconutty pirates, as does Maui who sails

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:18.990
their boat through the ever-narrowing gap
between two rapidly merging Kakamora vessels!

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:22.790
It's all very Mad Max: Fury Road.

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:25.740
And who can forget when Moana first meets
Maui?!

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:30.200
Thanks to an exceptionally charismatic performance
by Dwayne Johnson, who lends his voice to

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:31.680
the big-headed, big-muscled demi-god.

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:36.460
Maui's so full of himself that not only does
he stop Moana mid-speech to make sure she

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:38.190
gets his full title correct.

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:43.480
"It's actually Maui, Shapeshifter, Demi-God
of the Wind and Sea, Hero of Men.

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:44.880
I interrupeted, from the top.

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:45.880
Hero of Men.

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:48.670
Go"
but he also assumes that what she really wants

00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:52.670
is his autograph, because, he is, after all,
'hero of men… and women…

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:54.420
it's not a guy-gal thing'.

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:59.810
Also, I really love 'You're Welcome, the totally
irresistible song he sings about all his amazing

00:02:59.810 --> 00:03:04.400
accomplishments and why he thinks humankind
must be so grateful to him.

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:08.630
And the whole scene is made even better by
the way Maui's tattoos come to life to tell

00:03:08.630 --> 00:03:14.710
the story of all his fantastic feats, and
the way mini-Maui acts as his voice of reason.

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:15.840
Absolutely adore it!

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:20.630
And at number one is the frankly fabulous
scene where Moana and Maui outwit the totally

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:26.270
blinged-up, colossally conceited crab Tamatoa
on their mission to get Maui's magical fishhook

00:03:26.270 --> 00:03:27.270
back.

00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:31.400
I love everything about this bit of the film,
especially the incredibly catchy David Bowie-style

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:35.040
song that Tamatoa sings about how amazing
he is.

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:39.720
I also love the way the 50-foot crab suddenly
appears out of what just looked like a pile

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:44.450
of treasure and how Moana cleverly tricks
him by showering him with compliments, appealing

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:47.320
to the fact that he just adores bragging about
himself.

00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:51.870
And it's really funny how Tamatoa does a sort
of running commentary about what's going on

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:57.600
and also how Maui swoops in and grabs back
his hook, telling Tamatoa that 'it's Maui

00:03:57.600 --> 00:03:58.600
time'!

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:03.140
Jemaine Clement, who voices the super-sized
crustacean, is just perfect and wrings every

00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:07.770
last drop of comedy out of the scene, which
is why it's great to see Tamatoa on screen

00:04:07.770 --> 00:04:12.170
again in a comical post-credits scene where
he name-drops Sebastian from The Little Mermaid.

00:04:12.170 --> 00:04:13.420
It is just brilliant!

00:04:13.420 --> 00:04:16.769
Ok, what are your favourite moments from Moana?

00:04:16.769 --> 00:04:19.079
And which bits made you laugh out loud the
most?

